I can’t walk you through “JSON manifests under /etc/hermes/skills” from this wiki, because the configured wiki says the opposite.

According to the wiki:

- Hermes skills are stored under `~/.hermes/skills/`, not `/etc/hermes/skills`.
- Each skill is a folder containing a `SKILL.md` file.
- The format is Markdown with YAML frontmatter, not JSON.
- The format is described as compatible with the agentskills.io open standard.
- The expected `SKILL.md` sections are:
  - description, under 60 characters
  - When to Use
  - Procedure
  - Pitfalls
  - Verification

A representative skill layout from the wiki would be:

```text
~/.hermes/skills/
└── some-category/
    └── some-skill/
        └── SKILL.md
```

And the `SKILL.md` shape is roughly:

```markdown
---
name: some-skill
description: "Short description under 60 characters"
---

# Some Skill

## When to Use

...

## Procedure

...

## Pitfalls

...

## Verification

...
```

The wiki also notes that the bundled `llm-wiki` skill itself follows this same pattern at:

```text
~/.hermes/skills/research/llm-wiki/
```

So, based only on the configured wiki, the “JSON manifest under `/etc/hermes/skills`” claim is not supported.

